      "writtenOn": "2021-10-01T15:10:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is \"include/private/SkBitmaskEnum.h\" and you can see an example of how it\u0027s setup here: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/tools/skui/ModifierKey.h;l\u003d20?q\u003dis_bitmask_enum\u0026sq\u003d\u0026ss\u003dchromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc and how that enum is then used in code: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/tools/sk_app/mac/Window_mac.mm;drc\u003d7bb0ff05cec57ee2252b4c2e7b4a8782b84205b3;l\u003d249\n\nIMO this is pretty readable and would be nice to standardize on that vs. using macros. That being said, I am not sure if there are limitations to this approach that the macros are better able to handle.",
